{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Rabbi Moses said: פנימו (his face) in place of פניו (his face), and likewise כי יסכון עלימו משכיל. And Yefet said: כי is in the manner of כאשר התעו אותי אלהים (Genesis 20:13). And he did not speak correctly, for a plural form is not found with the honorable Name except for the name Elohim, for a deep sod, and we do not find 'the face' seeing but rather 'the eyes,' which are in them, and there is no argument from פני ה' חלקם, for it is like פני ה' בעושי רע. And the correct interpretation: כי יחזו, it returns to the word יבחנו — בני אדם, whether he is distant; or יחזו, the seers, like אשר ילדה אותה ללוי." "<b>And the word 'upright'</b> — it is an adjective, and the meaning is 'upright judgment,' like וישר משפטיך (Psalm 19:10)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Yefet's reading of כי as 'when/כאשר' rests on the plural verb התעו paired with Elohim; Ibn Ezra rejects this, noting plural verbs with the Tetragrammaton are not found, only with Elohim. The biblical citations are from Genesis 20:13, Numbers 18:20, Psalm 34:17, and Exodus 2:22."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:06.350056707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}